stical flora and fauna they as  well as the clans of indigenous people  who are resisting their incursions  seek your help for their own ends but  that's not all you also have something  you want from the island the cure for  the Malek or a mysterious plague  devastating your home beyond a vague  sense of awareness about its oppressive  legacy greed falls heavy-handed themes  never make way for anything more nuanced  or interesting sure it highlights the  exploitative behaviors of the Tali Mei  and bridge Alliance factions but their  actions are so mustache twirling  malicious that they become mere  caricatures of evildoers even your  companions and other characters are  cookie cutter emblems of their group  cieaura is the native princess who  wishes to seek peace for her clan petrus  is the religious t'lay may advisor with  tons of political savvy and curt is the  loyal headstrong mercenary whose stoic  demeanor can barely disguise his world  weariness God I'm not in need of your  protection no longer a child you know  greed Falls saving grace is that it's  role-playing systems are adequate and  the game's greatest strength is how well  it sticks to what is tried and tested it  features mechanical design that's common  in the genre but it's also savvy enough  to incorporate the best versions of  these elements at the beginning you're  given the choice of playing as one of  three character archetypes the melee  focused warrior the stealthy gunslinger  all the spell wielding tactician but  you're also given the flexibility to  break out of these standard classes  through an array of skill trees as you  progress through the game you can freely  invest hard earned points which opens up  a variety of methods you can approach  combat with and even how you resolve  quests as has become common in  open-world RPGs gratefull comes with a  crafting system and materials are in  abundance one constraint however is that  you can only craft upgrades to armor and  weapons you own 